The first implementation is now executable. It uses exact rational unit-disk coordinates and returns a symbolic congruence certificate; verification expands the rule and performs strict squared-distance checks, including cross-panel pairs. Initial checks confirm all four planted presets verify, with shipping candidates remaining compact (the current easy answer is 323 characters and the compact route is counted at 136 exact operations). I’m tightening the hand-scale demo before running the full 200,000-sample and adversary gates.
